# App Shell

**Shell** (Presentation) loads scenes. **Simulation** (ECS) is the run. There is no app-level state machine.

**Main** is the composition root. `AppScope` is the process scope: a prefab set as Root Lifetime Scope on `VContainerSettings` (Preloaded Assets). VContainer instantiates it once (DontDestroyOnLoad) and parents every scene scope to it. Simulation does not use the container.

## Elegant core (prefer this over jam GameDirector)

- `ShellService` is navigation only: `StartRun` / `RestartRun(RunLaunch)`, `GoToMenu`, `TryTakeLaunch`, `SplashShown`. It never calls `GameSession`.
- `TransitionService` owns every scene change: loading screen → teardown registry → Single load → `LoadingTasks.WaitAll` → hide. A failed task falls back to MainMenu. Scenes are never loaded additively on top of each other.
- `LoadingTasks` is the only way a scene says "wait for me": `Add(task, weight, label)`; failure = exception. `LoadingScreen` is a child of the `AppScope` prefab — there is no Loading scene.
- `GameEntry` (entry point of `GameLifetimeScope`) takes the launch from `ShellService` (or Normal) and adds `GameSession.Begin` to `LoadingTasks`. Temporary until 07 Ф1: `GameSession.Shutdown` is registered as an async teardown.
- `AppScope` registers `ShellService`, `TransitionService`, `LoadingTasks`, `SaveService`, `GameInput`, `LoadingScreen`. Each scene has its own `LifetimeScope` deriving from `LifetimeScope` directly (no parent reference needed). The slot file is `SaveService`; UI and `GameSession` do not touch it as a static.
- Temporary until 08 Ф4: Root holds only `Startup`, which takes `ShellService` from `AppScope` and opens the menu.
- `GameSession` lives in the Game scene: catalogs, `Begin` / `Apply` / `Shutdown`. It does not load scenes.
- `GameRun` (Game scope) turns the sim clock and game input on when `Begin` reaches Ready, and off when the run leaves. A game-scene machine is not built yet.
- Clock: `SimControl` + `SimClockCommand` in ECS — **no SimGate**, no `timeScale`
- MainMenu: splash then buttons live on `MainMenuFlow` in that scene. Buttons call `ShellService.StartRun`. Press any key plays once per process; `ShellService.SplashShown` remembers that across scene loads.
- VContainer stays in Presentation/Main. Never inside `ISystem`

## Do not treat as canon

Fat `GameDirector`, card Inject, soft restart via Find, economy pause via timeScale only, `Startup.Update`.

